        {
          "locator": "Finding and Fixing Calculation Instabilities",
          "source_id": "SRC-eadbb18f41"
        }
      ],
      "text": "Disconnected topology, coincident but unmerged nodes, unintended releases, missing supports, and crossing unconnected members are common instability or mechanism sources."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C3",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "locator": "Model debugging",
          "source_id": "SRC-2c4eebe57e"
        },
        {
          "locator": "Ill-conditioning theory",
          "source_id": "SRC-df393de74d"
        }
      ],
      "text": "Ill-conditioning and extreme stiffness contrasts should be distinguished from pure mechanisms because both can undermine result trust while requiring different model review."
    }
